body: "## Current hosted failure and canonical ownership\nAt default commit `133914ec3f7b39c00ae2434f138c004540d9e5a2`, the [gated sync job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/41297539843/job/124821446773) fails during `pm github import unbraind/pm-linear --state all --atomic --gate --dry-run --with-comments`:\n\n> GitHub issue #134 has multiple existing owners; import plan is not idempotent. No item was written for this issue.\n\nThe latest same-head sync check was still failed when refreshed at 2026-11-01 10:57 UTC. Canonical tracker inspection finds two closed records referring to the same source issue:\n- [pm-linear-github-18076be0368a-134](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/133914ec3f7b39c00ae2434f138c004540d9e5a2/.agents/pm/issues/pm-linear-github-18076be0368a-134.toon) has the explicit `gh:unbraind/pm-linear#134` tag and imported source description.\n- [pm-linear-ldqw](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/133914ec3f7b39c00ae2434f138c004540d9e5a2/.agents/pm/issues/pm-linear-ldqw.toon) starts its description with the same GitHub issue URL and retains implementation acceptance/evidence.\n\nExpected: one unambiguous importer owner for #134, while both records' useful knowledge, relationships and durable history remain intact. Actual: the guarded import refuses the ambiguous plan, blocking scheduled documentation synchronization. The refusal is appropriate; this is not evidence of data loss or a reason to weaken the guard.\n\n## Acceptance and limits\n- Reconcile importer ownership using supported PM operations, retaining both records and their provenance/history or performing an explicitly verified preservation migration.\n- Keep implementation/source-issue relationships without a second competing importer identity.\n- Demonstrate dry-run and applied import followed by an identical repeat produce no duplicate owner and no unintended item/history changes.\n- Keep atomicity and privacy gates enabled.\n\nThis report combines exact hosted failure with static canonical records; no live import, tracker mutation or local implementation was run. Checked all 197 current all-status GitHub items and 114 canonical PM `.toon` records before filing; no matching ownership-remediation issue found.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T22:08:15Z)\n>\n> Resolved by the triage PR that kept a single owner for GitHub issue #134. The scheduled sync rerun ([run 41523715457](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/41523715457)) passes the gated import step, with no multiple-owners refusal. The same run's later \"Verify repeat import is a no-op\" step still fails: that is pm-github pin lag, not ownership. This repo's workflows pin pm-github 2026.10.28, and the repeat-import fixes ship in 2026.10.30 and later (unbraind/pm-github#198, unbraind/pm-github#212). They arrive with the next Dependabot workflow bump."
